@thread missed_round
# en: The missed round
name [5ab68d] = 漏掉的巡房
# en: Sister Amaranth never misses a round. One night her lamp stayed dark.
premise [ce64fd] = 阿玛兰斯修女从不漏掉一次巡房。可有一夜，她的灯一直没亮。
# en: You went looking for Sister Amaranth when her lamp stayed dark, and found her grey with Lake Fever.
journal.1 [1c10bd] = 她的灯一直没亮，你去找阿玛兰斯修女，发现她染了湖热病，脸色发灰。
# en: You fetched the headmistress. Sister Amaranth didn't speak to you for a week, then told you to run faster next time.
journal.2 [b89e22] = 你去叫了院长。阿玛兰斯修女一个星期没跟你说话，然后吩咐你下次跑快点。
# en: You kept her secret and did the rounds she called out from her chair.
journal.3 [7ec1be] = 你替她保守秘密，照着她坐在椅子上报出的吩咐去巡房。
# en: You covered eight beds on your own, one remedy at a time.
journal.4 [a807a6] = 你一个人照看了八张病床，一剂药一剂药地来。
# en: Bed six owned up: a flat rock, a dare, and three friends coughing in secret. You brought them all down.
journal.5 [edd4b8] = 六号床说了实话：一块平石头、一个赌约，还有三个偷偷咳嗽的朋友。你把她们都领下了楼。
# en: You treated bed six for the chill she claimed, and her fever took its time.
journal.6 [eb8937] = 你照她说的着凉给六号床开了药，她的烧拖了好些天才退。
# en: Sister Amaranth came back a week too soon. You did the round with her, and she let you.
journal.7 [f01ee9] = 阿玛兰斯修女早回来了一个星期。你陪她巡了房，她也由着你。

@event infirmary_missed_round
# en: The Lamp That Went Out
title [6678b7] = 熄灭的灯
# en: The fever charm over the far bed has burned down to a red glow. It should have been turned an hour ago. Sister Amaranth does every round herself, and has never once missed one. Her lamp is dark.
text [980ef1] = 最里面那张床上方的退热符已经烧成一点暗红。一个钟头前就该转了。阿玛兰斯修女每一轮巡房都亲自去，从没漏过一次。她的灯是暗的。
# en: A dim infirmary ward at evening, a fever charm over the far bed glowing a dull red, a healer's desk lamp unlit.
scene [6a0e30] = 黄昏时昏暗的医务室病房，最里面那张床上方的退热符泛着暗红的光，医师桌上的灯没有点。
# en: Go and find her
opt.left.label [061e72] = 去找她
# en: The evening tray is still on the ward table, every bottle full. Her office door, at the back, is open a crack, and dark.
opt.left.say.1 [f6c902] = 晚间的药盘还搁在病房桌上，每个瓶子都是满的。后头她办公室的门开着一条缝，里面黑着。
# en: It isn't your ward
opt.right.label [c6562a] = 这不是你的病房
# en: You tell yourself she's only late. On your way out, the patient in the far bed is still awake, watching the dark.
opt.right.say.1 [a9f3b8] = 你告诉自己她只是来晚了。出门时，最里面那张床的病人还醒着，盯着黑暗。

@event infirmary_sister_fevered
# en: The Healer's Own Fever
title [3f2185] = 医师自己的高烧
# en: You find her in the little office behind the ward, upright in her chair, a cold compress on her own neck and the patient list in her lap. Her face is grey. "Lake Fever," she says. "From bed six. It's nothing. Go to bed."
text [14ad94] = 你在病房后面那间小办公室里找到她。她在椅子上坐得笔直，自己脖子上敷着冷毛巾，腿上摊着病人名单。她脸色发灰。“湖热病，”她说，“六号床传的。没什么。去睡觉。”
# en: A small office behind a hospital ward, a grey-faced healer upright in her chair with a compress on her neck and a list of patients in her lap.
scene [3c4215] = 病房后面的一间小办公室，面色发灰的医师在椅子上坐得笔直，脖子上敷着毛巾，腿上放着病人名单。
# en: Fetch the Headmistress
opt.left.label [f62300] = 去叫院长
# en: The headmistress comes in her dressing gown, and two healers from the village by morning. Sister Amaranth doesn't speak to you for a week. Then she thanks you, as an instruction: "Next time, run faster."
opt.left.say.1 [fc5764] = 院长穿着睡袍赶来，天亮前村里又来了两位医师。阿玛兰斯修女整整一周不跟你说话。然后她谢了你，用的是吩咐的口气：“下次跑快点。”
# en: Do the rounds she dictates
opt.right.label [069257] = 照她口述去巡房
# en: "Bed two, the blue bottle, half a spoon. Bed four, turn the charm. Bed six…" She stops. "Bed six will lie to you. Don't believe her." You do the rounds until midnight.
opt.right.say.1 [080508] = “二号床，蓝瓶子，半勺。四号床，转符。六号床……”她顿了一下，“六号床会骗你。别信她。”你一直巡到半夜。

@event infirmary_covering_rounds
# en: Eight Beds, One of You
title [49dfde] = 八张床，一个你
# en: {flag(rounds_secret): Sister Amaranth still can't stand, and is still giving orders from her chair.|The village healers are run off their feet, and Sister Amaranth, propped up in her chair, is giving them orders too.} Eight beds, eight remedies, one of you. A second-year with a burned hand wants to know if it will scar.
text [a5133b] = {flag(rounds_secret): 阿玛兰斯修女还是站不起来，还是坐在椅子上发号施令。|村里来的医师忙得脚不沾地，阿玛兰斯修女靠在椅子上，连他们也一起指挥。} 八张床，八种药，只有你一个人。一个手被烫伤的二年级生想知道会不会留疤。
# en: A row of infirmary beds at evening, a student in rolled-up sleeves measuring a remedy while a healer gives orders from a chair.
scene [856bc9] = 黄昏的一排病床，一个挽着袖子的学生正在量药，一位医师坐在椅子上指挥。
# en: Do every bed properly
opt.left.label [b70095] = 每张床都照顾周全
# en: Every bed, every spoon, every charm on the hour. The burned hand won't scar. At midnight the chair says, "Bed three. Well done," and then you hear her fall asleep sitting up.
opt.left.say.1 [4e9ba5] = 每张床、每一勺、每道符都准点照料到。烫伤不会留疤。半夜，椅子上传来一句：“三号床，做得好。”接着你就听见她坐着睡着了。
# en: You mix up beds three and five. Nobody notices but her. She makes you recite every dose on the ward back to her, with your eyes shut, before she lets you sleep.
opt.left.say.2 [0a4e69] = 你把三号床和五号床弄混了。除了她谁都没发现。她让你闭着眼，把病房里每一剂药量都背给她听，背完才放你去睡。
# en: Do the urgent ones, then revise
opt.right.label [7b2a0a] = 先顾急的，再去复习
# en: You see to the burns and the fevers and leave the rest for the morning. From the chair comes a small, disappointed silence.
opt.right.say.1 [469acd] = 你处理好烫伤和高烧，其余的留到早上。椅子那边传来一阵小小的、失望的沉默。

@event infirmary_bed_six
# en: Bed Six's Story
title [b331ff] = 六号床的说法
# en: Bed six is a second-year with Lake Fever, blue to the ears, who swears she never went near the lake. "I fell asleep in the bath," she says. From her chair, Sister Amaranth raises one eyebrow and keeps it there. The fever isn't breaking. A cure for a bath is not a cure for the lake.
text [0fe3df] = 六号床是个得了湖热病的二年级生，冻得耳朵发蓝，却发誓自己从没靠近过湖。“我是在浴缸里睡着了，”她说。阿玛兰斯修女在椅子上挑起一边眉毛，一直没放下来。烧退不下去。治浴缸的药，治不了湖。
# en: A shivering second-year in an infirmary bed with blue-tinged ears, insisting on something, while a healer watches sceptically from a chair across the ward.
scene [8f759c] = 医务室病床上一个瑟瑟发抖、耳朵泛蓝的二年级生正在坚持什么，病房另一头椅子上的医师满脸怀疑地看着。
# en: Get the true story out of her
opt.left.label [cf4525] = 套出她的实话
# en: It comes out in a rush: the flat rock, a dare, four of them. The other three are in her dormitory, coughing into their scarves so nobody will know. You fetch them down one by one. By midnight the ward is full, and all four fevers are breaking.
opt.left.say.1 [230782] = 实话一股脑儿涌了出来：那块平顶石，一个赌约，一共四个人。另外三个还躲在她们宿舍里，捂着围巾咳嗽，免得被人发现。你一个一个把她们领下来。到半夜病房住满了，四个人的烧都在退。
# en: She sticks to the bath. You treat her for the lake anyway, on Sister Amaranth's say-so, and on Thursday three more second-years turn up blue to the ears.
opt.left.say.2 [32d29b] = 她咬死了浴缸的说法。你还是照阿玛兰斯修女的吩咐按湖热病治她。到了星期四，又有三个二年级生冻得耳朵发蓝地找上门来。
# en: Treat what she tells you
opt.right.label [67acaa] = 照她说的治
# en: You dose her for a chill and get an early night. The fever takes three days longer than it should, and the chair across the ward watches every one of them.
opt.right.say.1 [e3829f] = 你按着凉给她配了药，自己早早睡下。烧比该退的晚了三天，病房那头的椅子一天不落地全看在眼里。

@event infirmary_own_prescription
# en: Her Own Prescription
title [b2ec64] = 她自己的药方
# en: Sister Amaranth is up a week too soon, grey at the edges, taking the tray out for the evening round as if nothing had happened. At bed two she sways and puts a hand on the rail. {flag(bed_six_truth): Four second-years sit up in their beds to watch.|The whole ward goes quiet.} Everyone looks at you.
text [7ded39] = 阿玛兰斯修女早了一个星期就下了床，脸色还泛着灰，端起药盘出去做晚间巡房，好像什么都没发生过。走到二号床时她晃了一下，伸手扶住床栏。{flag(bed_six_truth): 四个二年级生在床上坐起来看着。|整个病房一下子安静了。}所有人都看向你。
# en: A grey-faced healer in her apron holding a tray of tonics at an infirmary bedside, swaying slightly, while a student reaches to take the tray.
scene [e6bf63] = 一位脸色发灰、系着围裙的医师端着一盘药剂站在医务室床边，身子微微摇晃，一个学生伸手去接药盘。
# en: "Bed."
opt.left.label [09b6cc] = “上床。”
# en: You take the tray out of her hands and say it the way she says it to everyone else. She looks at you for a long moment. Then she goes to bed. You do the round. In the morning there's a card on the tray, in her square hand: "Bed four needs less."
opt.left.say.1 [2d0661] = 你从她手里接过药盘，用她对别人说这话的那种口气说了出来。她盯着你看了很久，然后回去躺下了。巡房你来做。第二天早上，药盘上多了一张卡片，是她方方正正的字：“四号床减量。”
# en: Walk the round beside her
opt.right.label [2bda60] = 陪她一起巡房
# en: You don't argue. You carry the tray and have each bottle ready before she reaches for it. At the last bed she sits down on the end of it, and lets you measure out her own dose. "Half a spoon," she says. "I'm not a horse."
opt.right.say.1 [447498] = 你没有争。你端着药盘，在她伸手之前就把每个瓶子递到她手边。到最后一张床，她在床尾坐下，让你给她自己量了一剂药。“半勺，”她说，“我又不是马。”

@thread red_ink
# en: Red ink
name [77bee0] = 红墨水
# en: Someone unsigned keeps marking your essays in red, and they're right.
premise [27df6f] = 有人不署名，总在你的论文上用红墨水批改，而且批得都对。
# en: Someone marked your essay in red ink, unsigned, and was right. You rewrote it and left it on the stair.
journal.1 [d71b70] = 有人用红墨水批改了你的论文，没有署名，而且批得对。你重写了一遍，把它留在楼梯上。
# en: The ink asked why you want to be good at this. You answered in the margin.
journal.2 [658ef1] = 红墨水问你为什么想把这件事做好。你在页边写下了回答。
# en: You hid on the landing and saw who took the essay: a first-year in robes two sizes too big.
journal.3 [7f3754] = 你躲在楼梯平台上，看见了来取论文的人：一个长袍大了两号的一年级生。
# en: The red ink is hers: a first-year who can't say a word in front of a room. She has a seminar on Thursday.
journal.4 [2f09dd] = 红墨水是她的：一个在一屋子人面前一个字也说不出的一年级生。她星期四有一场研讨课。
# en: On Thursday she spoke, all the way to the end.
journal.5 [c4d0f0] = 星期四，她开口了，一直讲到最后。

@event lecture_tower_red_ink
# en: Two Sets of Marks
title [8b53b5] = 两种批改
# en: Your returned essay has two sets of marks. The marker's, in polite pencil: "Good." And another, in red ink and unsigned, in a small round hand, savaging every paragraph and fixing three of them. The last line reads: "You can do better than good. Paragraph four proves it."
text [90c611] = 你拿回来的论文上有两种批改。批改老师用的是客气的铅笔：“好。”另一种是红墨水，没有署名，字小而圆，把每一段都批得体无完肤，还顺手改好了三段。最后一行写着：“你能写得比‘好’更好。第四段就是证明。”
# en: A student on a spiral stair reading an essay covered in neat pencil and, beneath it, furious corrections in red ink.
scene [580e72] = 一个学生坐在螺旋楼梯上，读着一篇论文，上面是工整的铅笔批注，底下是怒气冲冲的红墨水修改。
# en: Rewrite it properly
opt.left.label [ddefc9] = 认真重写
# en: You rewrite it twice. On the third morning you leave it on the second-floor stair, where you found the first. By evening it's gone.
opt.left.say.1 [874517] = 你重写了两遍。第三天早上，你把它放在二楼楼梯上，就是你捡到第一份的地方。到傍晚，它不见了。
# en: Bin it
opt.right.label [0a2a07] = 扔掉
# en: Good is good. You drop the red pages in the scorched-room bin, and feel a little foolish about how much you want to fish them out.
opt.right.say.1 [20fc67] = “好”就是好。你把那几页红字丢进烧焦教室的废纸篓，又有点难为情地发现，自己多想把它们捡回来。

@event lecture_tower_red_ink_reply
# en: A Question in the Margin
title [a0e86a] = 页边的问题
# en: The essay is back on the stair, bleeding red. Most of it is about your argument. At the bottom, smaller: "Why do you want to be good at this?" It's the first question the ink has asked.
text [630977] = 论文又回到了楼梯上，满纸红字。大部分是在说你的论证。最底下，字小了些：“你为什么想把这件事做好？”这是红墨水第一次提问。
# en: An essay left on a stone stair, its pages bleeding red ink, a single question written small at the bottom of the last page.
scene [bdf66c] = 一篇论文放在石阶上，纸页上满是红墨水，最后一页底部用小字写着一个问题。
# en: Answer it honestly in the margin
opt.left.label [e7dc4e] = 在页边老实作答
# en: You write three lines you'd never say aloud, and leave the essay on the stair. It's gone by noon. You spend the afternoon wishing you'd written two.
opt.left.say.1 [9ace38] = 你写下三行永远不会说出口的话，把论文留在楼梯上。中午前它就不见了。你一下午都在后悔，应该只写两行。
# en: Wait on the stair to see who takes it
opt.right.label [0b86d8] = 守在楼梯看谁来取
# en: You hide on the landing above. A first-year in robes two sizes too big gathers up the pages, reads the first line right there on the step, and makes a small, furious noise.
opt.right.say.1 [1ab338] = 你躲在上一层的平台上。一个穿着大两号袍子的一年级生把纸页收起来，就站在台阶上读了第一行，发出一声又小又气的哼声。
# en: You fall asleep on the stair. When you wake the essay is gone, and there's a note on your chest in red: "Paragraph six. Also, you snore."
opt.right.say.2 [5b6506] = 你在楼梯上睡着了。醒来时论文不见了，胸口上放着一张红字纸条：“第六段。还有，你打呼噜。”

@event lecture_tower_red_ink_front_row
# en: The Front Row
title [9d64e7] = 第一排
# en: You cut through the first-years' lecture on your way somewhere else. In the front row, alone, sits a first-year with red ink on her fingers. The lecturer asks her a question. She opens her mouth, and nothing comes out, and the hall waits until she looks at the floor. {flag(red_ink_glimpse): The robes are the ones from the stair, two sizes too big.|Her notes, you can see from the aisle, are perfect.}
text [04a185] = 你抄近路穿过一年级生的讲堂。第一排独自坐着一个一年级生，手指上沾着红墨水。讲师向她提问。她张开嘴，却一个字也说不出来，整个讲堂就那么等着，直到她低头看着地板。{flag(red_ink_glimpse): 那件袍子就是楼梯上那件，大了两号。|从过道上你就能看见，她的笔记完美无缺。}
# en: A lecture hall of first-years, one small student alone in the front row with red ink on her fingers, looking down at a page of perfect notes while the lecturer waits.
scene [8bd5f5] = 一间坐满一年级生的讲堂，一个瘦小的学生独自坐在第一排，手指沾着红墨水，低头看着一页完美的笔记，讲师在等她回答。
# en: Sit by her afterwards, and write
opt.left.label [3d6382] = 散场后坐到她旁边，用笔说话
# en: You sit down beside her after the hall empties and slide your last essay across, without a word. She writes on it for twenty minutes without looking up. At the bottom: "Seminar on Thursday. I have to speak. I can't."
opt.left.say.1 [8c43b8] = 讲堂散空后，你在她旁边坐下，一言不发地把你最近的论文推过去。她低着头在上面写了二十分钟。最底下写着：“星期四有研讨课。我得发言。我做不到。”
# en: Leave her the secret
opt.right.label [56b4e0] = 替她守着这个秘密
# en: You walk on, and leave your next essay on the stair as usual. It comes back with the usual red, and one line more at the bottom: "Seminar on Thursday. I have to speak. Please don't come."
opt.right.say.1 [531188] = 你走开了，照旧把下一篇论文放在楼梯上。它回来时还是满纸红字，最底下多了一行：“星期四有研讨课。我得发言。请别来。”

@event lecture_tower_red_ink_seminar
# en: Thursday's Seminar
title [ffda16] = 星期四的研讨课
# en: Thursday. The first-year stands at the seminar lectern with her paper in both hands and no voice at all. A dozen students wait. The lecturer looks at the clock. Her eyes find you at the back of the room.
text [111352] = 星期四。那个一年级生站在研讨课的讲台前，双手攥着讲稿，一点声音也发不出来。十几个学生在等。讲师看了看钟。她的目光在教室后排找到了你。
# en: A small seminar room, a first-year frozen at a lectern holding her paper in both hands, a dozen students waiting, one older student at the back half out of their seat.
scene [c9437a] = 一间小研讨室，一个一年级生僵在讲台前，双手攥着讲稿，十几个学生在等，后排一个高年级生半站起身。
# en: Stand up and argue with her paper
opt.left.label [785e58] = 站起来和她的论文辩论
# en: You stand and say her fourth paragraph is wrong. It isn't, and she knows it, and she's so annoyed she forgets to be frightened. She takes your objection apart for ten minutes. The room applauds, mostly for her.
opt.left.say.1 [593b7e] = 你站起来说她的第四段是错的。其实没错，她也知道，结果她气得忘了害怕，花了十分钟把你的反驳拆得七零八落。全场鼓掌，大半是为她。
# en: You stand and object, and your objection is bad, and she's too polite to say so out loud. She sits down without reading. Your essay comes back that week with one line of red: "Good try. Bad argument."
opt.left.say.2 [7d93e6] = 你站起来提出异议，可你的异议很烂，她又太客气，没当面说破。她没读就坐下了。那个星期你的论文发回来时，上面只有一行红字：“试得好。论证烂。”
# en: Offer to read it for her
opt.right.label [dde38f] = 提出替她念
# en: You walk to the front and hold out your hand. She shakes her head, then gives you the first page. You read the first paragraph aloud. She takes the second page back, and reads the rest herself, quietly, all the way to the end.
opt.right.say.1 [dbadbf] = 你走到前面，伸出手。她摇摇头，然后把第一页递给了你。你大声念完第一段。她把第二页拿了回去，自己轻声念完了剩下的，一直念到最后。

@thread late_bloomer
# en: The sweet shop's daughter
name [056316] = 糖果铺的女儿
# en: At home, the sweet-shop daughter has fire in her hands and nobody to teach her.
premise [4170c4] = 家乡糖果铺的女儿手里有火，却没有人教她。
# en: The sweet-shop daughter's sugar pan boiled on a cold stove. You taught her to breathe the heat down.
journal.1 [99ec4e] = 糖果铺女儿的糖锅在冷灶上沸了起来。你教她用呼吸把热压下去。
# en: Out past the fields, she learned to hold a flame the size of a fingernail.
journal.2 [01aa4d] = 在田地尽头，她学会了托住一朵指甲盖大的火苗。
# en: You promised her father you'd ask at the castle.
journal.3 [6addf1] = 你答应她父亲，会去城堡里问问。
# en: Her father asked what all that fire was for. You told him you didn't know.
journal.4 [cf91b6] = 她父亲问，那么多火是做什么用的。你告诉他，你也不知道。
# en: She bought the charm seller's grey glass bead, and the pans stayed cold.
journal.5 [71ea36] = 她买下了护符贩子那颗灰玻璃珠，糖锅从此一直是凉的。
# en: You told her the charm was only glass. She kept her coins.
journal.6 [39a79c] = 你告诉她那护符只是玻璃。她把钱收了回去。
# en: Frost ran from her feet across the square and caught a carter's arm in the trough. You got him out.
journal.7 [9b7881] = 寒霜从她脚下蔓过广场，把一个车夫的胳膊冻在了水槽里。你把他救了出来。
# en: You wrote to the castle about her.
journal.8 [2a2851] = 你给城堡写了信，讲了她的事。
# en: You left her your first practice candle, burned down to a stub.
journal.9 [54dca9] = 你把自己第一根练习用的蜡烛留给了她，已经烧得只剩一截。

@event home_market_late_bloomer
# en: The Cold Stove
title [ab26e7] = 冷灶
# en: The sweet shop is the one thing in town that hasn't changed. Then the owner's daughter, a year or two older than you, bangs down a ladle and swears, and the sugar pan on the cold stove boils over into caramel. There is no fire under it. Her father looks at you, then at your castle robes. "You're the one who'd know," he says quietly.
text [80d1ef] = 镇上只有这家糖果铺一点没变。接着，店主的女儿——比你大一两岁——把勺子往台上一摔，骂了一句，冷灶上的糖锅就溢成了焦糖。锅底下根本没有火。她父亲看看你，又看看你身上的城堡学院袍。“你是懂这个的人，”他低声说。
# en: The back of a small sweet shop, a copper sugar pan boiling over into dark caramel on a stove with no fire in it, a young woman staring at her own hands.
scene [ecd843] = 一间小糖果铺的后屋，一口铜糖锅在没有生火的灶上溢出深色的焦糖，一个年轻女人盯着自己的双手。
# en: Show her how to breathe it down
opt.left.label [1a87b0] = 教她把它压下去
# en: You show her the first thing anyone at the castle learns: breathe in for four, hold the heat, let it go for four. The pan stops seething. She looks at her hands as if they belonged to someone else.
opt.left.say.1 [673b25] = 你教她城堡里每个人学的第一件事：吸气数四下，把热憋住，再数四下放出去。糖锅不再翻腾了。她看着自己的手，好像那是别人的手。
# en: "It happens. It'll settle."
opt.right.label [6cc646] = “常有的事。会过去的。”
# en: Her father nods, glad to be told so. Behind him she scrapes the burned sugar out of the pan, very carefully, and doesn't go near the stove again.
opt.right.say.1 [d7c158] = 她父亲点点头，很高兴听到这句话。在他身后，她小心翼翼地把烧焦的糖刮出锅，再也没靠近灶台。

@event home_fields_bloomer_lessons
# en: Where Nothing Can Catch
title [aa3840] = 什么都烧不着的地方
# en: She's waiting past the last of the long rows, where the ground is all stones and nothing can catch, with a candle stub in each pocket. "Teach me something," she says. "Properly. Before you go back."
text [e00f96] = 她等在最后一垄地的外头，那里满地石头，什么都烧不着，她两个口袋里各揣着一截蜡烛头。“教我点什么，”她说，“正经教。趁你回去之前。”
# en: A young woman and a student in castle robes on a bare, stony patch past the last field row at sunset, the young woman holding a candle stub at arm's length, its flame far too tall.
scene [dde514] = 日落时分，最后一垄田外一块光秃秃的石头地上，一个年轻女人和一个穿城堡学院袍的学生，年轻女人伸直手臂举着一截蜡烛头，火苗蹿得太高。
# en: Teach her to keep a flame small
opt.left.label [04fe90] = 教她把火苗压小
# en: By sunset she can hold a flame the size of a fingernail for ten breaths. She counts every one of them out loud.
opt.left.say.1 [19772d] = 到日落时，她已经能让指甲盖大小的火苗稳住十次呼吸。她每一下都大声数出来。
# en: The candle goes off like a firework. You both lie in the grass laughing until the farmer shouts. "Next time," she says.
opt.left.say.2 [de9e7a] = 蜡烛像烟花一样炸开了。你们俩躺在草地上笑，直到农夫开骂。“下次吧。”她说。
# en: Spend the afternoon at home
opt.right.label [177620] = 下午留在家里
# en: You promise her next time. She shrugs, the way people do when they've stopped expecting things.
opt.right.say.1 [f41615] = 你答应她下次。她耸耸肩，就像人们已经不再指望什么时那样。

@event home_cottage_bloomer_father
# en: Sweets on the Step
title [a4badc] = 台阶上的糖
# en: Her father is at the door with a paper bag of the sweets you liked when you were small. He doesn't come in. "They take them young, at the castle, don't they," he says. "She's past it. So what is it for, all that fire, in a sweet shop?"
text [1d4d9f] = 她父亲站在门口，拿着一小纸袋你小时候爱吃的糖。他没有进来。“城堡收的都是年纪小的，是吧，”他说，“她已经过了那个年纪。那一身的火，在糖果铺里有什么用？”
# en: A worried shopkeeper at a cottage door holding a small paper bag of sweets, not stepping inside.
scene [9f38ed] = 一个忧心忡忡的店主站在小屋门口，拿着一小纸袋糖，没有进门。
# en: Tell him the truth
opt.left.label [48bf7e] = 对他说实话
# en: "I don't know what it's for," you tell him. "I don't think anyone does, at her age." He thanks you for not lying, and leaves the sweets on the step.
opt.left.say.1 [98beb1] = “我不知道有什么用，”你告诉他，“到了她这个年纪，我想谁也不知道。”他谢谢你没有骗他，把糖留在了台阶上。
# en: Promise to ask at the castle
opt.right.label [aafec0] = 答应去城堡问问
# en: His face does something complicated. "Would you," he says, not quite a question. You hear yourself promise. The sweets taste exactly as they used to.
opt.right.say.1 [e74743] = 他的脸上掠过很复杂的神情。“你会吗。”他说，不太像是在问。你听见自己答应了。那些糖的味道和从前一模一样。

@event home_market_bloomer_charm
# en: A Lid on the Pot
title [f09a76] = 锅上的盖子
# en: In the market you find her at the charm seller's stall. He's holding up a grey glass bead on a cord. "Lumenhold-blessed," he's saying. "Smothers it, like a lid on a pot. No more flares, no more fuss." It's plain glass; you can see that from here. She's counting out her savings.
text [7577dc] = 你在集市上卖护身符的人的摊子前找到她。他正举着一颗系着绳子的灰玻璃珠。“流明堡加持过的，”他说，“能把它闷住，就像给锅盖上盖子。再不会冒火，再不会出乱子。”那就是一颗普通玻璃珠，你站在这儿都看得出来。她正在数自己的积蓄。
# en: A market charm seller holding up a grey glass bead on a cord to a young woman counting coins from her apron.
scene [97e8d2] = 集市上卖护身符的人举着一颗系着绳的灰色玻璃珠，一个年轻女人正从围裙里数出硬币。
# en: Let her believe in it
opt.left.label [f3c641] = 让她信下去
# en: You say nothing. She buys it and puts it on. It's only glass, but she believes in it, and the sugar pans stay cold all week. She looks lighter, and smaller.
opt.left.say.1 [b3f436] = 你什么都没说。她买下它戴上了。那不过是玻璃，可她信它，糖锅一整个星期都是冷的。她看上去轻松了些，也小了些。
# en: Tell her it's only glass
opt.right.label [2d22ae] = 告诉她那只是玻璃
# en: "It's glass," you tell her. "You did the hard part yourself, out past the fields." The charm seller gives you the look of a man revising his prices. She puts her coins back in her apron, slowly.
opt.right.say.1 [45bba8] = “那是玻璃，”你告诉她，“最难的那部分，是你自己在田那头做到的。”卖护身符的人看你的眼神，像是在重新盘算价钱。她慢慢把硬币放回了围裙口袋。
# en: She buys it anyway. "Easy for you," she says, not unkindly. "You get to go back."
opt.right.say.2 [d6500c] = 她还是买了。“你说得轻巧，”她说，并没有恶意，“你还能回去。”

@event home_market_bloomer_ice
# en: Ice in the Square
title [44b78b] = 广场上的冰
# en: Not ten minutes later, a shout from the square. The horse trough has frozen solid, with a carter's arm in it to the elbow, and she's standing beside it white with panic. Frost is creeping across the cobbles from her feet.
text [6aaab7] = 不到十分钟，广场上传来一声大喊。饮马槽冻得结结实实，一个车夫的胳膊冻在里面，一直冻到手肘。她站在旁边，吓得脸色发白。霜正从她脚下爬过石板路。
# en: A market-square horse trough frozen solid around a carter's arm, a panicking young woman beside it and frost spreading across the cobbles.
scene [4e5996] = 集市广场上的饮马槽冻得结结实实，把一个车夫的胳膊封在里面，一个惊慌的年轻女人站在一旁，霜在石板路上蔓延。
# en: Break the ice by hand
opt.left.label [fe2922] = 用手砸开冰
# en: You hammer at the ice with a cobble until it gives with a crack like a door. The carter pulls his arm free, swearing, mostly at the trough.
opt.left.say.1 [280b1c] = 你抄起一块铺路石砸冰，直到它像一扇门一样咔嚓一声裂开。车夫抽出胳膊，骂骂咧咧，主要是在骂那个饮马槽。
# en: You get him free in the end, but the ice takes the skin off your knuckles doing it. You'll feel that trough for days.
opt.left.say.2 [f780c2] = 你最后还是把他弄了出来，可冰把你的指节磨掉了一层皮。那个饮马槽你得疼上好几天。
# en: Talk her down so it melts
opt.right.label [2bd1f0] = 安抚她让冰化开
# en: "Four in. Hold. Four out." Her breath slows, and the ice goes grey, then soft, then water. The carter stares at his arm, and then at her.
opt.right.say.1 [62e526] = “吸气四下。憋住。呼气四下。”她的呼吸慢下来，冰变灰，变软，化成了水。车夫盯着自己的胳膊，又盯着她。
# en: It takes an hour, three kettles from the inn and a carter who will tell this story for years.
opt.right.say.2 [25f257] = 花了一个钟头、旅店的三壶热水，还造就了一个会把这事讲上好多年的车夫。

@event home_cottage_bloomer_letter
# en: A Flame That Stays
title [62c792] = 不灭的火苗
# en: {flag(bloomer_damped): She comes by one evening, the grey bead on its cord. "I know it's only glass," she says. "I keep it in my pocket anyway." She lights a candle with her finger, small and steady, to show you.|She comes by one evening with a candle she lit at noon and has kept burning, small and steady, all day. "Look," she says. "It stays."}
text [de4168] = {flag(bloomer_damped): 一天傍晚她来了，那颗灰珠子系在绳上。“我知道那只是玻璃，”她说，“可我还是揣在口袋里。”她用手指点燃一支蜡烛给你看，火苗小而稳。|一天傍晚她来了，手里拿着一支中午点着、一直烧到现在的蜡烛，火苗小而稳。“你看，”她说，“它不灭。”}
# en: A young woman at a cottage table at evening, a small steady candle flame burning on the tip of her finger.
scene [a44cc7] = 傍晚，一个年轻女人坐在小屋的桌旁，指尖上燃着一朵小小的、稳定的烛火。
# en: Write to the castle for her
opt.left.label [3d556e] = 替她给城堡写信
# en: {flag(bloomer_promise): You keep your promise to her father and write to the castle that night|You write to the castle that night}: what she can do, what she learned with no teacher but you, and that some people come late to things. You pay the postage; she walks it to the post office herself.
opt.left.say.1 [e70f80] = {flag(bloomer_promise): 你遵守了对她父亲的承诺，当晚就给城堡写了信|当晚你给城堡写了信}：她能做什么，她在除了你之外没有老师的情况下学会了什么，还有，有些人就是来得晚一些。邮费你付了；信是她自己走去邮局寄的。
# en: Leave her your practice candle
opt.right.label [e7919c] = 把你的练习蜡烛留给她
# en: {flag(bloomer_promise): You never did ask at the castle. Instead you leave her|You leave her} the practice candle you've had since your first week, the one you learned on, burned down to a stub. A month later a letter comes with a drawing of the stub, still lit.
opt.right.say.1 [364432] = {flag(bloomer_promise): 你到底没去城堡问。你把|你把}入学第一个星期就开始用的那支练习蜡烛留给了她，你就是用它学会的，如今只剩一截蜡烛头。一个月后来了一封信，里面画着那截蜡烛头，还亮着。
